       LOOK 4.8.1 · inspect the computer

LOOK
  lk [THING]           inspect a path, command, port, or process
  lk [PATH]            smart filesystem view
  lk FILE              interactive file card + paged preview
  lk detail [PATH]     detailed view
  lk dirs [PATH]       directories
  lk files [PATH]      files
  lk tree [PATH]       tree
  lk recent [PATH]     newest first
  lk size [PATH]       size-oriented
  lk run [PATH]        what can I do here? (project is an alias)

INSPECT
  lk up / ports        what is listening? (services is an alias)
  lk port NUMBER       inspect one listening port
  lk process TERM      find a running process (proc)
  lk processes         browse/filter processes · Y copies PID (procs)
  lk pid NUMBER        inspect one process ID
  lk git [PATH]        repository status
  lk machine / gpu     machine capabilities
  lk disk              disk usage
  lk net               browse network addresses · Y copies IP
  lk tailscale         tailnet status
  lk env / path        environment / PATH diagnostics
  lk why COMMAND       explain command resolution

AI / OLLAMA
  lo [ASK]             Ollama chat / optional first prompt
  lo search [ASK]      chat with Ollama web search
  lo @HOST [ASK]       use another Ollama host for this session
  lo --conservative      read/search only for this session
  lo --workspace         workspace tools + explicit path grants (default)
  lo --power             shell tools · known read-only inspections auto-run;
                         other commands use native once/session confirmation
  lo --unsafe            unrestricted shell for this session
  lk o --no-start ...    never start a missing local server
  lk ollama            Ollama + selected-host status
  lk ollama models     model panel · Enter select · X enable/disable
  lk ollama test       benchmark LOOK-selected model
  lk ollama test --all compare enabled installed models
  lk ollama host       list saved + reachable Ollama hosts
  lk ollama host NAME  make NAME the persistent default
  lk ollama host local return to localhost
  lk ollama host NAME URL
                       save URL as NAME and select it
  lk ollama host forget NAME
                       forget a saved remote host
  lk ollama share      share local Ollama inside the tailnet
  lk ollama share status
                       Tailscale Serve + LOOK proxy status
  lk ollama share off  stop the tailnet Ollama share
  lk ollama key        securely save the Ollama web-search key
  lk ollama key status report key configuration; never reveal it
  lk ollama access      show persistent LO capability profile
  lk ollama access MODE set conservative/workspace/power/unsafe

MEMORY + CRAFT
  lk memory            inspect Living Memory: core summary, durable domains/atoms,
                       recent conversation, candidates, compiler diagnostics
                       candidates are cheap hypotheses; durable memory must earn promotion
  lk memory add TEXT   add a candidate memory (default importance 60)
  lk memory add TEXT --importance N
                       add with importance 1–100
  lk memory forget TEXT
                       remove matching candidate + durable atomic memories
  lk forget TEXT       short form of memory forget
  lk memory compact    force domain/core summary recompilation now
  lk memory prune      remove known reasoning/meta/environmental artifacts
  lk memory clear      clear this user's LO memory
  lk memory clear-summary
                       clear compiled summary text; durable atoms remain
  lk memory clear-recent
                       clear literal cross-session conversation continuity
  lk clear-memory      short form of memory clear
  lk skills            show LO's bundled + learned assistant craft
  lk skills version    show skills schema / bundled pack version
  lk skills update [FILE]
                       update Bundled craft; preserve Learned craft
  lk skills add TEXT   manually add a reusable learned skill
  lk skills forget TEXT
                       remove matching locally learned skills
  lk skills clear-learned
                       clear only locally learned skills
  lk skills path       print the editable skills file path
  lk skills state      show reinforcement confidence and feedback hits
                       auto-learning runs in workspace/power/unsafe; conservative never writes skills
                       natural praise/criticism may trigger conservative background reflection

MAKE
  lmk FILE.ext         create an empty file · undoable
  lmk DIR/             create directory + enter it · undoable
  lmk -f NAME          force file when the name is ambiguous
  lmk -d NAME          force directory + enter it
                       extensionless names ask: [d]irectory or [f]ile

MEDIA
  lk media             show current player / state / track
  lk media toggle      play / pause, then show current state
  lk media next        next track, then show current state
  lk media prev        previous track, then show current state
  lk media stop        stop/pause, then show current state
  mm / mn / mp         fast aliases: toggle / next / previous

ACCESS + PERMISSIONS
  lk access            show persistent/session filesystem grants
  lk access personal   permanently allow Desktop/Documents/Downloads read/write
  lk access add PATH [read|write]
                       permanently extend LO filesystem reach
  lk access remove PATH
                       revoke one persistent path grant
  lk access clear      clear persistent + current-session grants
                       outside-workspace tool calls can also grant once/session/always interactively
  lk ollama access     separate capability profile: conservative/workspace/power/unsafe

LO PERSONALITY + THINKING
  lk personality       show personality choices
  lk personality NAME  lo · robot · max · philosopher
  lk thinking          show thinking depth
  lk thinking MODE     light · adaptive · deep
  lk think-display     show thinking presentation
  lk think-display MODE compact · full · quiet
  lk settings [SEARCH] searchable control room for all settings

SERVICES + TAILNET SHARING
  lk services                  local/running/share status
  lk services discover         discover Mercury Writer when possible
  lk services set mercury PORT configure Mercury Writer explicitly
  lk services share all        expose configured running services to tailnet
  lk services share comfy      share one service
  lk services unshare all      remove LOOK service shares
  lk share                     friendly alias for `lk services share all`
  lk share status              service/share status
  lk share off                 unshare all LOOK services

  Default LOOK service ports stay separate:
    Ollama   → LOOK proxy HTTPS 11435
    ComfyUI  → HTTPS 8188
    Mercury  → configured/discovered port
  Tailscale Serve remains tailnet-only; LOOK does not use Funnel.

VISION + GENERATIVE MEDIA
  lk vision IMAGE [QUESTION]
                       send a local image to the selected Ollama vision model
  lo ... IMAGE.png    vision-capable models attach explicit image paths automatically
  lk share            share all configured/running LOOK services over Tailscale
  lk services         inspect/configure/share local services
  lk comfy            status for optional/managed ComfyUI
  lk comfy start|stop|restart
                       manage LOOK-installed ComfyUI process
  lk comfy discover   scan home + mounted drives for old Comfy/A1111 model libraries
  lk comfy bootstrap  rerun managed GPU install/model setup
  lk comfy host URL   configure local/remote Comfy API endpoint
  lk comfy workflow PATH
                       configure an API-format workflow using __PROMPT__,
                       __NEGATIVE__, and optional __SEED__ placeholders
  lk generate PROMPT  queue generation, save output under ~/Pictures/LOOK,
                       and preview the first result when configured

SCHEDULER
  lk schedule                 list persistent jobs
  lk schedule in 30m PROMPT   run once later
  lk schedule every 2h PROMPT recurring interval
  lk schedule daily 08:00 PROMPT
                              recurring local-clock job
  lk schedule pause|resume|remove|run ID
                              manage jobs; resident LOOK AI dispatches them

DESKTOP BRIDGE
  lk open PATH          open local path in preferred/default graphical app
  lk preview PATH       Quick Look on macOS; default/preferred app elsewhere
  lk reveal PATH        reveal path in Finder/file manager
  lk apps               show preferred apps by category
  lk apps video vlc     set preferred video app
  lk apps pdf system    return PDF handling to OS default
  categories            browser · editor · image · pdf · video · audio
                        LO uses open_path / preview_path / reveal_path rather than
                        inventing platform-specific app commands

SYSTEM
  lk home              friendly LOOK home screen
  lk doctor            check the environment
  lk settings [SEARCH] searchable settings control room
  lk profile           portable LOOK identity status
  lk profile backup [DEST] [--keep N]
                       create/remember rotating profile backups
  lk profile export [ZIP]
                       create one migration archive
  lk profile restore SOURCE [--yes]
                       restore profile with safety snapshot
  lk skills export [FILE]
                       export only locally learned skills
  lk feedback          show sound/motion settings
  lk feedback sound on|off
  lk feedback motion off|subtle|normal
  lk sound             quick sound toggle
  lk config            show installed paths + state
  lk secrets           secrets status (never contents)
  lk undo              undo last safe local filesystem action
  lk uninstall         remove Future Crash + LOOK owned files
  lk version           print version
  lk help              this complete command/key glossary
  LOOK_CLASSIC=1 lk    use the frozen classic presentation

FILE ACTIONS
  lcp [PATH]           LOOK-assisted copy
  lmv [PATH]           LOOK-assisted move
  lscp [PATH]          LOOK-assisted scp
  lrm [PATH]           LOOK-assisted remove (confirmed)
  lmk PATH             make directory path · undoable
  mkd DIR              make directory and enter it
  lk undo              undo newest safe LOOK filesystem transaction
  lk undo list         inspect READY/BLOCKED transaction history
  lk undo skip         abandon newest BLOCKED record; filesystem unchanged

SHORTCUTS
  CANONICAL  lk detail · lk dirs · lk files · lk tree · lk recent · lk size
  FAST       lkl · lkd · lkf · lkt · lkr · lkz   (LOOK namespace; always installed)
  OPTIONAL   l · ll · ld · lf · lt · lr · lz · lh · fc
             installed only when collision policy allows; `force` may reclaim fc
  lk         smart view            zll WORD jump + look
  lk home    LOOK home             lk o     Ollama chat
  f          find anywhere → LOOK  fcr      Future Crash
  cdl WORD   jump + details        fznv     fuzzy edit
  rs         reset ritual          rb       reload zsh
  webterm    terminal over Tailscale
  lk shortcuts                    inspect/set shortcut policy
  command ls                      always the real Unix ls
  terminal title shows owner: ● LOOK · ● LO · ● FUTURE CRASH · ◌ FUTURE CRASH SHELL

LIVE FILTER / SELECTION
  Type       filter immediately
  j/k/↑/↓    move selection in browse/select; while typing a filter use J/K or ↑/↓
  Tab/⇧Tab   mark / unmark highlighted item
  A          mark all matches / clear all marked matches
  Enter / →  open file / enter folder
  ← / <      go up one filesystem directory
  E          edit
  O          open with another application
  B          copy file object(s) to desktop clipboard
  C / M / R  Copy To / Move To / remove
  L          hand persistent working set to a new LO session
  X          clear persistent working set
  Y          copy absolute path(s) as text
  P          print absolute path + exit
  G          exit LOOK and make this the shell's directory
  Esc        clear / back / cancel
  q          quit

FILE CARD
  j / k / ↑ / ↓       scroll preview
  Space / b            page forward / back
  Enter                 open
  E / O                  edit / open with
  B / Y / P              clipboard file / copy path / print path
  M / C / S / R          move / copy / scp / remove
  L                        hand selected/marked paths to LO
  q / Esc                quit

HELP PAGER
  j / k / ↑ / ↓       line down / up
  Space / b            page forward / back
  PgDn / PgUp          page forward / back
  g / G                beginning / end
  q / Esc              quit
.fi
